use std
into layout.amni
lang amni
Amni-Drive's refined, zero-void, concave-arc hugging cockpit layout and driver-ergonomic button-placement engine. Every interactive surface (Map, Media, 3D Dash Drum, Voice/Nav rail) maximizes display area; secondary telemetry (Speed, Weather icon, Clock) sits compactly in geometric spandrel corners calculated from exact chord geometry so nothing ever overlaps or clips an arc. All coordinates and sizes are 32-bit floats in logical pixels.
Struct `Rect` holds `x`, `y`, `w`, and `h` as 32-bit floats.
Struct `Circle` holds `cx`, `cy`, and `r` as 32-bit floats.
Struct `HitButton` holds `id` as a 32-bit integer, `rect` as a `Rect`, and `primary` as a boolean.
Struct `Pod` holds `kind` as a 32-bit integer (0 map, 1 media, 2 speed_badge, 3 weather_badge, 4 apps_badge, 5 clock_badge, 6 drum_3d), `shape` as a 32-bit integer (0 rect, 1 circle, 2 hex, 3 capsule, 4 crescent_left, 5 crescent_right, 6 crescent_bottom), `rect` as a `Rect`, `circle` as a `Circle`, `cutout` as a `Circle`, `safe_rect` as a `Rect`, and `chamfer` as a 32-bit float.
Struct `CockpitPlan` holds `screen_w` and `screen_h` as 32-bit floats, `layout_id` as a 32-bit integer, `dock_rect` as a `Rect`, `stage_rect` as a `Rect`, `portrait` as a boolean, `dock_bottom` as a boolean, `buttons` as a growable list of `HitButton`, and `pods` as a growable list of `Pod`.
Function `make_rect` takes `x`, `y`, `w`, and `h` as 32-bit floats and returns a `Rect`.
Function `rects_overlap` takes two `Rect` values `a` and `b` and returns true if their interiors strictly overlap by more than 0.5 pixels on both axes.
Function `rect_inside` takes `inner` and `outer` as `Rect` values and returns true if `inner` lies inside `outer` within 0.5 pixel tolerance on all four edges and has positive width and height.
Function `inscribe_circle` takes a `Rect` `r` and returns a `Circle` centered in `r` with radius equal to half of the smaller of `r.w` and `r.h`.
Function `circle_safe_rect` takes a `Circle` `c` and returns the chord-safe inner `Rect` centered at `c.cx`, `c.cy` with width and height equal to `c.r * 1.4142`.
Function `make_pod` takes `kind` and `shape` as 32-bit integers, `r` as a `Rect`, and `cutout` as a `Circle`, returning a `Pod`.
- When `shape` is 1 (circle): set `circle` to `inscribe_circle` of `r`, `safe_rect` to `circle_safe_rect` of that circle, and `chamfer` to 0.
- When `shape` is 2 (hex): set `chamfer` to `min(r.w, r.h) * 0.07` clamped between 12 and 24, and inset `safe_rect` by `chamfer * 0.55` on all sides.
- When `shape` is 3 (capsule): set `chamfer` to `min(min(r.w, r.h) * 0.28, 44.0)` and inset `safe_rect` horizontally by `min(r.w * 0.08, chamfer * 0.5)` and vertically by 8.
- When `shape` is 5 (crescent_right): set `chamfer` to 24.0. Compute `left_clear = max(r.x + 12.0, cutout.cx + cutout.r + 12.0)` so `safe_rect` sits strictly to the right of the concave cutout arc (`x = left_clear`, `y = r.y + 16.0`, `w = max(40.0, r.x + r.w - left_clear - 14.0)`, `h = max(40.0, r.h - 32.0)`).
- When `shape` is 4 (crescent_left): set `chamfer` to 24.0. Compute `right_clear = min(r.x + r.w - 12.0, cutout.cx - cutout.r - 12.0)` so `safe_rect` sits strictly to the left of the cutout (`x = r.x + 14.0`, `y = r.y + 16.0`, `w = max(40.0, right_clear - (r.x + 14.0))`, `h = max(40.0, r.h - 32.0)`).
- When `shape` is 6 (crescent_bottom): set `chamfer` to 24.0. Compute `top_clear = max(r.y + 12.0, cutout.cy + cutout.r + 14.0)` so `safe_rect` sits strictly below the concave cutout arc (`x = r.x + 18.0`, `y = top_clear`, `w = max(40.0, r.w - 36.0)`, `h = max(40.0, r.y + r.h - top_clear - 16.0)`).
- Otherwise (rect): `safe_rect` equals `r` and `chamfer` is 0.
Function `compute_cockpit` takes `screen_w`, `screen_h`, `min_hit`, `gutter`, and `pad` as 32-bit floats, `layout_id` as a 32-bit integer (0 twin chrono, 1 solar binnacle, 2 orb center, 3 horizon dials, 4 hex cockpit, 5 capsule deck, 6 asym triptych, 7 tri cockpit, 8 split, 9 full map, 10 drum 3d), `dock_mode` as a 32-bit integer (0 auto LHD rail, 1 bottom dock, 2 RHD rail), and `swap_map_media` as a boolean, returning a `CockpitPlan`.
First decide orientation: `portrait` is true when `screen_h` is greater than `screen_w * 1.05`. `dock_bottom` is true when `portrait` is true or `dock_mode` is 1.
Compute the slim driver-ergonomic dock and stage rectangles:
- When `dock_bottom` is true: `dock_h` is `max(min_hit + 8.0, 66.0)` clamped to at most `screen_h * 0.15`. `dock_rect` sits along the bottom edge `(pad, screen_h - dock_h - pad, screen_w - 2.0 * pad, dock_h)`. `stage_rect` fills `(pad, pad, screen_w - 2.0 * pad, screen_h - dock_h - 2.0 * pad - gutter)`.
- When `dock_bottom` is false: `dock_w` is `max(min_hit + 12.0, 74.0)` clamped to at most `screen_w * 0.12`. If `dock_mode` is 2 (RHD), `dock_rect` sits on the right edge `(screen_w - dock_w - pad, pad, dock_w, screen_h - 2.0 * pad)` and `stage_rect` fills `(pad, pad, screen_w - dock_w - 2.0 * pad - gutter, screen_h - 2.0 * pad)`. Otherwise (LHD default), `dock_rect` sits on the left edge `(pad, pad, dock_w, screen_h - 2.0 * pad)` and `stage_rect` fills `(pad + dock_w + gutter, pad, screen_w - dock_w - 2.0 * pad - gutter, screen_h - 2.0 * pad)`.
Place the six driver-priority buttons inside `dock_rect` with ids 1 (NAV), 2 (MEDIA), 3 (APPS), 4 (VOICE, primary true), 5 (3D/VIEW), and 6 (SET):
- Along the dock's long axis, divide `long_span - 5.0 * btn_gap` into 6 equal slots where `btn_gap` is `max(gutter * 0.65, 7.0)` reduced only if needed so every slot stays at least `min_hit * 0.85` (never below 48 pixels). Inset each button by 3 pixels on the cross axis.
Next, place primary interactive pods and spandrel corner badges inside `stage_rect` (`sx = stage_rect.x`, `sy = stage_rect.y`, `sw = stage_rect.w`, `sh = stage_rect.h`, `g = gutter`). Let `zero_c` be a zero `Circle`, `k_left` be 1 if `swap_map_media` else 0, `k_right` be 0 if `swap_map_media` else 1.
- Layout 0 (`TWIN_CHRONO`): Maximized dual circular dials filling full height with tight geometric V-spandrel badges that never clip either dial.
  - If `portrait`: top circular pod (`k_left`, `dial_d = min(sw * 0.94, (sh - g) * 0.495)` centered horizontally at `sy`) and bottom circular pod (`k_right`, same `dial_d`, centered horizontally at `sy + sh - dial_d`). Tuck compact `speed_badge` (92 by 40 capsule) at top-left `(sx + 4, sy + 4)` and `weather_badge` (92 by 40 capsule) at top-right `(sx + sw - 96, sy + 4)`.
  - If landscape: compute `dial_d = min(sh * 0.96, (sw - g) * 0.50)`. Place left circular pod (`k_left`, square `dial_d` by `dial_d` vertically centered at `sx` on left) and right circular pod (`k_right`, square `dial_d` by `dial_d` vertically centered at `sx + sw - dial_d` on right). Compute badge height `bh = clamp(sh * 0.10, 38.0, 48.0)` and badge width `bw = clamp(sw * 0.21, 108.0, 158.0)`. Place `speed_badge` capsule centered horizontally in the top V-spandrel `(sx + (sw - bw) * 0.5, sy + 2.0, bw, bh)` and `weather_badge` capsule centered horizontally in the bottom V-spandrel `(sx + (sw - bw) * 0.5, sy + sh - bh - 2.0, bw, bh)`.
- Layout 1 (`SOLAR_BINNACLE`): ZERO wasted left void! Giant circular map hugs the driver rail on the left, while a sweeping concave-arc Media Wing fills the ENTIRE right side with a guaranteed uncarved `safe_rect`!
  - If `portrait`: giant top circular `map` (`dial_d = min(sw * 0.94, sh * 0.50)` centered horizontally at `sy + 2`). Its circle is `(cx, cy, r)`. Below it, place a sweeping `crescent_bottom` interactive `media` wing starting at `y_wing = cy + r * 0.42` down to `sy + sh` (full width `sw`), with `cutout = Circle(cx, cy, r + g)` — its `safe_rect` automatically begins below `cy + r + g + 14` so album art and controls NEVER touch the map circle! Tuck compact `speed_badge` (`w = 104, h = 42` capsule) in the top-left spandrel `(sx + 6, sy + 6)` and `weather_badge` (`w = 104, h = 42` capsule) in the top-right spandrel `(sx + sw - 110, sy + 6)`.
  - If landscape: `map_d = min(sh * 0.97, sw * 0.56)`. Anchor the giant circular `map` directly adjacent to the left edge of `stage_rect`: `cx = sx + map_d * 0.5`, `cy = sy + sh * 0.5`, `r = map_d * 0.5`. Define `cut = Circle(cx, cy, r + g)`. Place a MASSIVE sweeping `crescent_right` interactive `media` wing from `x_wing = cx + r * 0.44` to `sx + sw` (full height `sh`), using `cut` so its left border gracefully curves around the entire right hemisphere of the map while its `safe_rect` stays strictly clear of the arc! Tuck compact `speed_badge` (`w = clamp(sw * 0.125, 108.0, 144.0), h = 42` capsule) into the top-left spandrel `(sx + 4, sy + 4)` and compact `weather_badge` (`w = clamp(sw * 0.115, 96.0, 132.0), h = 42` capsule) into the bottom-left spandrel `(sx + 4, sy + sh - 46)` and compact `clock_badge` (`w = 108, h = 38` capsule) into the top-right corner of the media wing `(sx + sw - 118, sy + 10)`.
- Layout 2 (`ORB_CENTER`): Same zero-void giant left-anchored circular map (`map_d = min(sh * 0.96, sw * 0.54)`) + sweeping `crescent_right` media wing + compact top-left `speed_badge` and bottom-left `weather_badge`.
- Layout 3 (`HORIZON_DIALS`): Full-bleed rectangular `map` filling `stage_rect`, with compact floating `speed_badge` + `weather_badge` pills top-left and a floating circular `media` orb bottom-right (`clamp(min(sw, sh) * 0.40, 128.0, 210.0)`).
- Layout 4 (`HEX_COCKPIT`): Zero passive widget column! Two crisp chamfered octagonal interactive pods filling 100 percent of `stage_rect`: `k_left` (`60%` of `sw - g`) and `k_right` (`40%` of `sw - g`) in landscape (or `58%` over `42%` in portrait), plus compact `speed_badge` (`w = 108, h = 38`) and `weather_badge` (`w = 96, h = 38`) nestled cleanly inside the top-right bevel margin of the left pod (`y = sy + 14`).
- Layout 5 (`CAPSULE_DECK`): Sleek architectural rounded pods (`shape = 3`, radius clamped to at most 44px): if `portrait`, `map` (`60%` height) over full-width interactive `media` (`40%` height); if landscape, `map` (`60%` width) beside interactive `media` (`40%` width), with compact `speed_badge` + `weather_badge` pills at top-right of map.
- Layout 6 (`ASYM_TRIPTYCH`): Golden-ratio interactive split (`62%` `k_left`, `38%` `k_right`, both `shape = 0`) with compact `speed_badge` + `weather_badge` pills.
- Layout 7 (`TRI_COCKPIT`): `k_left` (`58%`) and `k_right` (`42%`) with compact `speed_badge` + `weather_badge` pills.
- Layout 8 (`SPLIT`): 55 percent `k_left` and 45 percent `k_right` (both rect).
- Layout 9 (`FULL_MAP`): Single rectangular `map` pod filling `stage_rect` plus compact top-right `speed_badge` and `weather_badge` pills.
- Layout 10 (`DRUM_3D`, or any other value): Single full-stage `drum_3d` (`kind = 6`, `shape = 0`) filling `stage_rect` where the primary interactive app rolls on a giant 3D cylindrical dial recessed into the dash, flanked by compact top-left `speed_badge` (`w = 112, h = 40`) and top-right `weather_badge` (`w = 104, h = 40`) pills!
Function `validate_cockpit` takes a `CockpitPlan` and returns 0 if every button is inside `dock_rect`, no two buttons overlap, every button has width and height at least 48 pixels, `dock_rect` and `stage_rect` do not overlap, and every pod's `rect` lies inside `stage_rect`; otherwise return a nonzero error code (1 button out of dock, 2 buttons overlap, 3 button too small, 4 dock overlaps stage, 5 pod out of stage).
